+## Submission authority
+
+The [writer epoch](../concepts/identity.md#writer-epoch) says which attempt may commit. It cannot show that a submitter *is* that attempt. Anyone who may inspect the Execution can read the current Activation ID and epoch, and a caller who copied them into an envelope would pass the fence without being the attempt the fence protects. The current attempt needs something to present that nobody else can produce.
+
+**Submission authority** is the Kernel-issued proof that a submitter is the current Runtime attempt of an unresolved exchange. The Kernel issues it with the attempt, hands it to the Driver together with the Activation, and the Driver presents it back with the attempt's Outcome. Nothing that inspection, the Activation or an envelope reveals can reproduce it, and inspection never exposes it.
